//! apkaudio-contracts — the Rust mirror of `@apkaudio/contracts`.
//!
//! `topics`, `identity`, and `time` are HAND-WRITTEN (behavior, not shape)
//! and kept honest against the TypeScript implementations by the shared
//! golden-vector files under `contracts/vectors/`. `gen/` is cargo-typify
//! output regenerated by `pnpm gen` — never edited by hand. `heartbeat` and
//! `device_record` are thin wrappers: re-exports of the generated types plus
//! the behavior half of each contract (LWT helper, v40 mapping).
//!
//! `broker_auth` is here rather than in an agent because it is a policy every
//! agent must share — which environment variables carry the bus credentials —
//! and the crate's no-client-library rule is what keeps it from becoming a
//! connection helper. It returns the pair; the caller applies it.
//!
//! `spog_envelope` is a READ-ONLY mirror of a foreign contract rather than of
//! `@apkaudio/contracts`: SPOG's protobuf value envelope, decoded so a
//! translator can hear a console without either side learning the other's
//! codec. It is here for the same reason `broker_auth` is — every process that
//! listens to that bus must read it the same way — and it obeys the same
//! no-client-library rule: bytes in, a struct out.
//!
//! `broker_backoff` is the other half of that same split: `broker_auth` says
//! who an agent is to the broker, `broker_backoff` says what it costs when the
//! broker says no. It names no client library either — its drain is generic
//! over `Iterator<Item = Result<T, E>>` — so the pacing rule lives here once
//! instead of in the 35 agent loops that each got it wrong the same way.

/// Which edition of these contracts a binary was built against (PLAN-3407.01).
///
/// THE PACKAGE VERSION, read by cargo, not a second number to keep in step.
/// A plugin publishes it as `build.contract_version` in its `incoming/api`, so
/// a reader can tell a plugin built against an older topic set from a current
/// one once plugins are released separately. The Python mirror carries the
/// same string as `apkaudio_contracts.CONTRACT_VERSION`, and
/// `python/tests/test_contract_version.py` fails when the two differ.
pub const CONTRACT_VERSION: &str = env!("CARGO_PKG_VERSION");

pub mod gen;

pub mod topics;

pub mod broker_auth;

/// The brand's visual constants, read from `contracts/tokens/brand.json`.
/// Here for the same reason `broker_auth` is: more than one top-level directory
/// must agree on the value exactly, and this is the only layer all three
/// languages already import. See `002_🏛⚖📜 Philosophy/Styles/where a design token
/// lives.md` for the decision and the category error it tolerates.
pub mod tokens;

pub mod broker_backoff;

pub mod spog_envelope;

pub mod identity;

pub mod time;

pub mod heartbeat;

pub mod agent_counters;

/// The scan narration line, and the level vocabulary that is NOT `LOG_LEVELS`.
/// Here rather than in the orchestrator because the producer spells the level
/// as a `&str` and two front-end files tone on it, and until PLAN-1040.01 the
/// only declaration of the set anywhere was a comment on the line that wrote it.
pub mod scan_log_line;

/// The `Agent/state` topic every protocol hunter reports itself on. Here for
/// the same reason `broker_auth` is: it was a convention held privately by two
/// crates out of twenty-three, and a convention is what the third crate
/// disagrees with. See the module docs for what it deliberately does not move.
pub mod agent_state;

/// Which controls are reading the bench clock out loud, as the one retained
/// document KOMAND reads back on connect. Here rather than in the agent for
/// the reason `agent_state` is: the retain flag and the clear-on-empty are the
/// contract, not the call site's to get right. PLAN-736.01.
pub mod komand_clock;

/// Every bare-metal item's `incoming/` and `outgoing/` landing spots.
pub mod baremetal_io;

/// What an agent says about itself on its own loopback (`GET /status`,
/// `GET /telemetry`), the five-state vocabulary — running, serving, failed,
/// unknown, stub — and the rule that derives the word from the packet counter,
/// never from the claim; plus `agent.toml` and [`embedded_manifest!`]. The
/// server is `apk-plugin-runner`'s; this is what it serves. ROAD-3472.
pub mod baremetal_telemetry;

/// `APK_SERIAL_SETTINGS` — the operator's declared serial line settings, one
/// grammar for PLUGIN.VISA and PLUGIN.SERIAL_COM, which each held a copy of
/// the parser (2026-10-30 audit). Vector-held with the Python twin.
pub mod serial_settings;

/// The `nmos` device table row schema shared by PLUGIN.NMOS and PLUGIN.NMOS_CONTROL
/// (2026-10-30 audit). Vector-held (`vectors/nmos_rows.json`).
pub mod nmos_rows;

/// PLUGIN.NDI's `System/Vendors/NDI` tree as a versioned schema (2026-10-30 audit).
pub mod vendors_ndi;

/// What may be written on a machine's `outgoing/command` (power, a named
/// command, a deploy), who may write it, and the retained answer. PLAN-3394.01.
pub mod machine_command;

/// Trunk-Caster on the bus: the Ward-Beck line, frame/port/trunk identities,
/// panel labels, the caster's command envelope and every `trunk` /
/// `trunk_sim` topic. `contracts/TRUNK.md`; vectors `vectors/trunk.json`. ROAD-3440.
pub mod trunk;

/// The behavior half of `ControlValue` -- the constructors that make the
/// envelope buildable from Rust at all, and the rendering rule. `gen/` had the
/// shape and nothing had the behavior, which is why nothing published one.
pub mod control_value;

pub mod device_record;
/// Active since / inactive since — the schemaVersion 2 document on
/// `Discovery/{protocol}/{deviceId}`, written on a transition only. PLAN-3318.01.
pub mod discovery_presence;
/// The proof beside the silent status: `Discovery/{protocol}/{deviceId}/verified`,
/// `{verifiedAt, by}`, restated by the agent on each successful re-verification
/// and read by the engine's lifecycle `check`. ROAD-3437.
pub mod discovery_verified;
/// A sighting, said as the one document the registry reads — the retained
/// `Discovery/{protocol}/{deviceId}` write that thirteen hunters each needed
/// and none had. Here rather than in an agent for the same reason `identity`
/// is: two agents deriving different ids for one device is the bug that
/// module already fixed once.
pub mod device_publish;


/// Taking one item off the bench to prove it still works — the retained
/// withdrawal, the momentary run, the depths a run may reach and the per-check
/// table it answers with. Here rather than in an agent for the reason the
/// module's own docs give: ten of the twenty-nine crates link no MQTT client,
/// so the thing that runs their tests is not them, and a contract is the only
/// place a rule shared by an agent and its supervisor can live. PLAN-459.01.
pub mod self_test;

/// What an agent says about a device it can see NOW — the `-1` sentinel on
/// `last_online`, the `online_since` stamp beside it, and the register that
/// keeps the stamp from moving. Here rather than in an agent because eleven
/// hunters and the orchestrator have to agree on what `-1` means; a private
/// convention is what the twelfth disagrees with.
pub mod presence;
